<p>US Secretary of State Marco Rubio used the Munich Security Conference to insist the US remains committed to NATO, while urging European allies to carry more of the alliance’s load. He paired reassurance about transatlantic unity with pointed messages about Europe aligning more closely with US priorities. From Munich, Rubio headed to Central Europe, including stops in Slovakia and Hungary, as Washington looks to deepen cooperation with governments led by conservative figures described as having warm ties to President Donald Trump. Even with Rubio’s reassurances, some European audiences remained unsure how durable US policy will be, with coverage noting that his polite tone may not sway leaders already preparing to build greater independence and capability of their own.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DLas2Zxe2EvDJpLIYouf5N5XPFP9h2v6f956KooSVC2Gnbr3IjdJoLvRIoBVm8qkcy8YR8Wh-x0KhyZF74O6TILWwvGKLbMaI5eo7NSf_aRds5uMx-phnX1EUk4kp6XGtzUDiRex_uTt4RbTOkf2PrYLu6Y4j3oH1phZJ5UT46YwOHaXmZVpzbeFEl-hemSYZLR2juUx-sinox9Gfmabi45qWdu76gOPMq54JMuX2OMVKWgJDQ3Vhmv03-2_nhtexmm471tXHvab67NWbg' alt='U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio boards a plane departing Bratislava Airport in Slovakia, Feb. 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Budapest kickoff: Rubio opened a trip through Slovakia and Hungary by pledging deeper cooperation with both countries, whose conservative leaders have warm ties to President Donald Trump.</li><li>Bratislava stop: A day after Munich, Rubio made a brief stop in Slovakia’s capital to push back on talk of a US exit from NATO and to urge Europe to take a stronger role.</li><li>Conditional reassurance (Semafor): Rubio said the US isn’t looking to abandon the transatlantic alliance — as long as Europe moves closer to the American worldview.</li><li>Munich framing (Reuters via Al-Monitor): Rubio called the US the “child of Europe,” offering unity and reassurance while also criticizing allies after a year of turmoil under President Trump.</li><li>Conference backdrop (Reuters via Al-Monitor): Munich attendees tried to project more European independence and strength, even as they worked to keep the US alliance intact.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Secretary of State Marco Rubio: In Bratislava, after the Munich Security Conference, Rubio dismissed speculation about a US retreat from NATO and urged Europe to take on a stronger role. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/from-central-europe-rubio-rejects-nato-exit-talk-calls-for-stronger-european-role/33679038.html'>Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty</a>)</li><li>US State Department: The department said the Slovakia-Hungary trip would focus on energy cooperation and other bilateral issues, including NATO commitments. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rubio-to-visit-eastern-europe-bolster-ties-with-pro-trump-leaders/article70636116.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Munich coverage (Semafor): Semafor’s coverage suggested Rubio’s careful, reassuring tone may not be enough to erase European doubts about the reliability of US policy. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/15/2026/rubio-strikes-polite-tone-in-munich-but-europe-likely-not-convinced'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>European security conference context (Reuters via Al-Monitor): At Munich, Reuters described European powers as trying to show more independence and strength while still working to keep the US alliance intact under President Trump. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/rubio-casts-us-child-europe-critical-friend-allies-0'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rubio-to-visit-eastern-europe-bolster-ties-with-pro-trump-leaders/article70636116.ece'>Rubio to visit Eastern Europe, bolster ties with pro-Trump leaders</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/15/2026/rubio-strikes-polite-tone-in-munich-but-europe-likely-not-convinced'>Rubio strikes polite tone in Munich, but Europe likely not convinced</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/from-central-europe-rubio-rejects-nato-exit-talk-calls-for-stronger-european-role/33679038.html'>From Central Europe, Rubio Rejects NATO Exit Talk, Calls For Stronger European Role</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/rubio-visits-central-europe-to-bolster-ties-with-pro-trump-leaders'>Rubio visits central Europe to bolster ties with pro-Trump leaders</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-rubio-slovakia-hungary-orban-fico/'>Rubio visits Slovakia and Hungary to bolster ties with pro-Trump leaders</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/rubio-casts-us-child-europe-critical-friend-allies-0'>Rubio casts US, the &#x27;child of Europe&#x27;, as critical friend to allies</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>